## Context

Child of tracker 0613 (goal 1), gap A. `Ticket-ref: tickets/0613`. Sibling of
0630 (gap B's `UNINSTALL.md` draft), same pattern: 0629 attributed the four
network lookups and established that all four trace to one cause — the
default-`true` update check's single `fetch()` — and explicitly left "no new
upstream filing here" as out of its own scope, naming 0613's Action 3
("decide the upstream form of gaps A and B") as the ticket that owns it. This
ticket is that decision and the resulting draft, for gap A only.

**Form, argued against `GOVERNANCE.md`'s "Form follows the measured
asymmetry"**: contained defect with a failing test → PR (two precedents,
#27/#28, merged verbatim); design-sized → issue the author files himself. The
update check is not a defect — `server.ts:186-187`'s comment gives a real
reason for it (manual installs have no other update channel) — it is a
default the maintainer chose deliberately. Changing a deliberate default is a
product decision, not a one-line fix with an obviously-correct answer, so
this is design-sized: **issue, not PR.**

## Relevant files

- `verification/ISSUE-DRAFT-0634.md` — the drafted issue, staged not sent.
- `bench/results/0629-gap-a/README.md` and `syscall-shape.json` — the
  measurement the draft cites.
- `fork/src/lib/update-check.ts`, `fork/src/config.ts`, `fork/src/server.ts`
  — the reviewed-SHA source the draft's file:line citations point at
  (`fork/` itself is gitignored and regenerated per `UPSTREAM`).

## Actions

1. Draft the issue at `verification/ISSUE-DRAFT-0634.md`, matching the
   format and voice of `verification/ISSUE-DRAFT-0530.md` (the one prior
   filed-from-measurement draft in this repo): a short "staged, not sent"
   preamble arguing form, then `## Title` / `## Body` verbatim-ready content.
2. Cite evidence by file:line from a real built `fork/` at the reviewed SHA,
   not from memory or a fetched copy — re-derived in this session (see
   0613/0629 log entries 2026-09-04) and cross-checked against 0629's own
   citations; one two-line drift found (`capabilities.ts` desktop-probe loop
   at `:53`, not `:55-56`), named in the draft itself rather than silently
   corrected.
3. Propose a fix shape (default off, or first-run consent) without demanding
   either — the maintainer decides, per this repo's own upstream posture.
4. Do **not** open the real GitHub issue. This repo's convention (SYNC.md,
   GOVERNANCE.md, and every prior design-sized item) is that the harness
   prepares the record; the author sends it, on his own authorization, per
   action.

## Test

No code changes; nothing here is unit-testable. The check this ticket
actually needs is a read-through: does every file:line citation in the draft
resolve, in a real `fork/` checkout at `UPSTREAM_REVIEWED_SHA`, to what the
draft says is there? Verified during Action 2 above (see the ticket log).

